$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for N-Boc-Protected o-Aryl
Anilines. A mixture of N-Boc-protected o-bromoaniline 1 (1 equiv), the
corresponding boronic acid (1.6 equiv),
tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)-palladium (5 mol %), and potassium carbonate
(2.5 equiv) in toluene/ EtOH (4/1) (0.1 M) was stirred at 80 °C under an
argon atmosphere for 2-4 h. The reaction mixture was diluted with AcOEt,
washed with water and brine, dried over MgSO4, and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The residue was purified by column chromatography
(hexanes/AcOEt) to afford the desired product. tert-Butyl
(2-(Furan-3-yl)phenyl)carbamate. The product was obtained following the
general procedure (1.8 mmol scale) as yellow solids (444 mg, 95%) after
purification by column chromatography. mp 62-64 °C (hexanes/EtOAc); Rf =
0.32 (5% AcOEt/hexanes); 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 8.05 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 1H),
7.59-7.57 (m, 1H), 7.56 (dd, J = 1.6, 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.31 (ddd, J = 8.2,
8.2, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 7.27-7.23 (m, 1H), 7.07 (ddd, J = 7.5, 7.5, 1.2 Hz,
1H), 6.62 (br s, 1H), 6.56 (dd, J = 1.7, 0.9 Hz, 1H), 1.50 (s, 9H); 13C
NMR (CDCl3) δ 152.9, 143.8, 140.1, 135.7, 129.7, 129.0, 128.4, 123.2,
122.5, 120.1, 111.1, 80.5, 28.3; IR (KBr) νmax 3422, 3348, 2978, 2920,
1728, 1589, 1516, 1501, 1447, 1366 cm-1; MS (FAB) m/z 259 (M+), 203 (M
-t-Bu + H), 186 (M -t-BuO), 159 (M -Boc); HRMS-ESI (m/z) calcd for
C15H18NO3 [M + H]+ 260.1281, found 260.1280. Anal. Calcd for C15H17NO3:
C, 69.48; H, 6.61; N, 5.40. Found: C, 69.26; H, 6.73; N, 5.26.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
