$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure G: Suzuki-Miyaura coupling.
A solution of heteroaryl halide (1.0 equiv), aryl boronic acid (1.0
equiv), Pd(PPh3)4 (2.5 mol%), and Cs2CO3 (2.5 equiv) in 2:1 EtOH/H2O (1.0
M) was stirred at 80 °C. After cooling to 23 °C, H2O was added. The
aqueous phase was extracted with EtOAc (3x). The combined organic layers
were washed with brine, dried over Na2SO4, filtered and evaporated under
reduced pressure. The crude material was purified by silica gel column
chromatography (hexanes/EtOAc). 2-(2-Methoxyphenyl)-6-methylpyridine
(S22): Prepared by the general procedure G from 2-bromo-6-methylpyridine
(1.0 mL, 8.8 mmol, 1.0 equiv), 2-methoxyphenylboronic acid (1.3 g, 8.78
mmol, 1.0 equiv), Pd(PPh3)4 (0.25 g, 0.22 mmol, 2.5 mol%) and Cs2CO3 (7.2
g, 17.6 mmol, 2.5 equiv), purified by column chromatography
(hexanes/EtOAc) and isolated as a pale yellow oil (1.6 g, 95% yield). IR
(thin film) 3058, 2999, 2958, 2939, 2835, 1587, 1575, 1492, 1463, 1448,
1433, 1244, 1024 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.74 (dd, J = 1.6, 7.2
Hz, 1H), 7.61-7.57 (m, 2H), 7.35 (ddd, J = 2.0, 7.6, 8.4 Hz, 1H),
7.09-7.05 (m, 2H), 6.99 (brd, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 3.84 (s, 3H), 2.62 (s,
3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 158.12, 157.04, 155.62, 135.89, 131.31,
129.76, 129.73, 122.17, 121.28, 121.20, 111.48, 77.48, 77.16, 76.84,
55.74, 24.88; HRMS (MALDI) calc’d for C13H14NO [M + H]+: 200.1070, found:
200.1070.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
